Stop allocating two Locations and two events for every boat, every tick.

AbstractBoat#tick unconditionally built a Bukkit Location for the current position, cast the boat to
a CraftEntity, fired VehicleUpdateEvent, optionally fired VehicleMoveEvent, and then allocated a
second Location for lastLocation. VehicleUpdateEvent's result is discarded outright and
VehicleMoveEvent only reports movement, so with neither listened for none of that is observable.

Boats are common - transport, ice roads, boat farms - and this is per boat per tick, so it adds up
in a way the event name does not suggest.

lastLocation is set to null rather than left stale in the unlistened branch. The existing code
already skips VehicleMoveEvent when lastLocation is null, so a plugin registering later seeds
cleanly on its first tick instead of receiving one bogus move spanning the entire period nothing
was listening.

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/vehicle/boat/AbstractBoat.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/vehicle/boat/AbstractBoat.java
@@ -277,11 +277,26 @@
+        final boolean vehicleUpdateListened = VehicleUpdateEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0;
+        final boolean vehicleMoveListened = VehicleMoveEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0;
+        if (vehicleUpdateListened || vehicleMoveListened) {
         org.bukkit.Location to = CraftLocation.toBukkit(this.position(), this.level(), this.getYRot(), this.getXRot());
         org.bukkit.entity.Vehicle vehicle = (org.bukkit.entity.Vehicle) this.getBukkitEntity();
-        new VehicleUpdateEvent(vehicle).callEvent();
-        if (this.lastLocation != null && !this.lastLocation.equals(to)) {
+        if (vehicleUpdateListened) new VehicleUpdateEvent(vehicle).callEvent();
+        if (vehicleMoveListened && this.lastLocation != null && !this.lastLocation.equals(to)) {
             new VehicleMoveEvent(vehicle, this.lastLocation, to).callEvent();
         }
         this.lastLocation = vehicle.getLocation();
+        } else {
+            this.lastLocation = null;
+        }
